EM='expecting_mother'; XM='experienced_mother'; NM='new_mother'; PU='parent_unspecified'
Q=[
(120,'',NM,'looking_back','success_story',['birth_stories','horror_stories','contrary','first_pregnancy'],"When I was pregnant I didn’t know what to expect. And all I heard was horror stories. And that’s fair those stories exist, but it isn’t always like that. I kept waiting for the horror to start and it never did.","Two months postpartum, writing for first-time mothers about an easier pregnancy than she was told to expect."),
(120,'',NM,'looking_back','pain',['horror_stories','birth_fear','stock_lines'],"one thing I had a hard time with was constant anxiety that it would turn horrible at any minute because I had always been told it would be.","What being told the worst cost her in pregnancy."),
(120,'ouiu0gq',NM,'looking_back','fear',['nausea','comparison_other_pregnancies','family'],"I kept being super anxious in the first trimester that I would wake up one day and not be able to stop the nausea or puking because my sister was pregnant and ahead of me by 4 months and that was her experience but it never happened.","Measured her pregnancy against her sister's."),
(120,'oum6gp5',NM,'looking_back','tried_failed',['partner_role','preparation'],"My husband and I went to couples therapy during pregnancy with the mindset of preparing for having our first baby. To try and set us up for success.","Asked what helped her prepare.",True),
(121,'',XM,'second_pregnancy','success_story',['second_pregnancy','pregnancy_with_toddler','comparison_other_pregnancies'],"I’m now 11 weeks pregnant with my second and holy moly some moments I even forget I’m pregnant, which would have sounded impossible last time around. I do have an 8 month old I take care of, but he’s a pretty chill baby.","Second pregnancy soon after a very hard first."),
(121,'',XM,'second_pregnancy','purchase',['diet_rules','price_value','partner_role','nausea'],"So… I DoorDash. Yes it’s expensive. But guess what, I’m able to keep my protein up.","Stopped cooking through nausea this time; husband away for work for days."),
(121,'',XM,'second_pregnancy','belief',['exercise_in_pregnancy','guilt','previous_pregnancy'],"Last time I definitely got trapped in the “all or nothing” thinking and it made me feel so guilty for being on the couch instead of spending 45 minutes at the gym like I was used to.","What she changed about her expectations this time."),
(121,'',XM,'second_pregnancy','desire',['previous_pregnancy','information_gap','trust_people'],"if there was ANYTHING that could have helped me last time, I wish someone would have said something.","Why she wrote up what she is doing differently."),
(122,'',NM,'looking_back','purchase',['hypnobirthing','birth_course','birth_preparation'],"We prepared for this by doing a hypnobirthing course, I also tried to stay active and do some specific stretches. I drank all the teas and ate the dates","Her preparation for the first birth, in a country with private maternity care."),
(122,'',NM,'looking_back','pain',['birth','not_told','professionals'],"I had never had one before so I didn't know they could be so painful. Luckily she was quick and it didn't take long so I got through it. But I wish she would have explained that it could be painful.","Nobody warned her what an exam in labour would feel like.",True),
(123,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','others_said',['stock_lines','birth','professionals'],"By the way, if you’ve never had anyone tell you ‘just breathe’ or ‘don’t scrunch your face’ while you’re actively in labor…🙄🙄🙄","Days after a birth that went far from her plan."),
(123,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','regret',['birth_plan','plan_b'],"I really wish I’d realized how much that threw my entire birth plan out the window.","A condition found on arrival changed the whole birth.",True),
(125,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','others_said',['c_section','not_told','stock_lines'],"I’ve been told you feel like a purse getting dug around in, but I never acknowledged the pain I’d feel.","Hours after an unplanned surgical birth.",True),
(126,'',XM,'looking_back','belief',['social_pressure','feeding','birth_preference'],"I feel like there’s so much social pressure to give birth unmedicated and breastfeed. It’s amazing and a wonderful thing when you can, but it’s not for everyone and I am learning to accept that it’s okay that it wasn’t for me.","Mother of two, a month after her second birth."),
(126,'',XM,'looking_back','others_said',['feeding','friend_pressure'],"I have recently been pressured by a friend to keep going and try to pump as long as I can.","Feeding went the same way with both babies."),
(126,'',XM,'looking_back','failure_story',['feeding','previous_pregnancy','comparison_other_pregnancies'],"It was so disheartening because the same thing happened with my first pregnancy.   \nI was hoping this time would be my do over.","The second baby was meant to be a different feeding experience."),
(126,'',XM,'looking_back','fear',['epidural_decision','guilt'],"I feel weak because I got the epidurals out of fear, I’m deathly afraid of feeling crowning. Props to those who go without it but I couldn’t and because of that I felt terrible, like I took the easy way out.","Guilt over pain relief in both births.",True),
(126,'ov4u2il',XM,'looking_back','success_story',['feeding'],"Switching to formula was definitely so freeing!","Reply to another second-time mother."),
(127,'',EM,'third_trimester','tried_failed',['research_overload','birth_stories','reassurance'],"I searched Reddit like a madwoman, hoping to find some encouraging stories, but most of what I found was really scary. So I hope my experience helps someone else.","After a frightening scan finding, wrote the encouraging story she had looked for.",True),
(128,'',XM,'looking_back','tried_failed',['postpartum_recovery','what_to_buy','hospital'],"I purchased 2, from \"popular baby brands\" (not allowed to use actual names) and in the end the hospital one was the one that worked the best (for me anyway)","Mother of three on recovery gear after a planned surgical birth."),
(128,'',XM,'looking_back','belief',['research','birth_stories','reassurance'],"back then I used to stalk this thread regularly looking for advice because I was no anxious and wanting to know what to expect.","Why she now posts her own advice.",True),
(129,'',EM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','others_said',['stock_lines','family','dismissed','birth'],"After sharing this with family and friends many people joke and just say “well you won’t remember it in a few weeks anyways!” Or “nothing ever goes according to plan” or my favorite response from a male family member “I’ve had kidney stones I’ve heard that’s pretty similar to the pain of an unmedicated birth”. I’ve never felt more dismissed","First-time mother on what family said after a birth that went against her one-line plan.",True),
(129,'',EM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','advice_given',['stock_lines','visitors'],"please be mindful for your words to recent mothers who have delivered, their experience is significant to them whether or not you deem it to be.","Her closing advice to readers.",True),
(130,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','advice_given',['hospital_bag','sleep','hospital'],"It’s basically impossible to sleep in the hospital. Bring earplugs or noise cancelling headphones for white noise. They also come in like every hour for checks.","One week after her first birth, listing what she learned."),
(130,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','belief',['first_two_weeks','sleep','guilt','hospital'],"I ended up using the nursery for a few hours to get some sleep. She was cluster feeding the second night and I had slept about 4 hours over 48 hours and I was starting to feel WEIRD. I felt a little guilty sending her away, but knew I needed sleep to take care of her.","On the second night in hospital."),
(130,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','advice_given',['hospital_bag','feeding','not_told'],"Bring snacks. I didn’t realize how hungry you get when you start producing milk.","Something nobody had told her."),
(130,'',NM,'newborn_0_2_weeks','fear',['birth_fear','previous_hospital'],"I should also note, I was TERRIFIED of labor and delivery due to previous hospital experiences and abdominal surgery.","Her fear going into a first birth.",True),
]
